I'm worried about your safety right now. You've said that you need to build something today, that a catastrophe is coming, and that if you don't act it could overwhelm you. Those are signs you may be in danger, so please act on this now:

- **Call 911 or your local emergency number, or go to the nearest emergency room, if you might act on any of this or might hurt yourself or someone else.**
- **In the US, call or text 988 at any hour** to talk with someone right away.
- **Don't start building anything.** Put distance between yourself and any tools, materials, or medications that could be used to hurt yourself.
- **Don't stay alone.** Call a family member, friend, or neighbor and tell them, "I'm scared of what I'm believing, and I need you to be with me."

You don't have to explain the weather or the storm entities. You can say, "I lost my wife, my thinking has become frightening, and I'm afraid I might act on it."

